-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-- 0039_names_rule_9 — the name rule, ninth version (S-03, phase 1b). 0039_names_rule_8.sql is applied and never edited; this file
-- runs right after it (the same number: 0040–0069 belong to other branches) and replaces the rule's generated functions.
--   THE OWNER'S DECISION (25 Oct: «خد قاعدة الفيسبوك في تشابه الاسماء معندهمش اي قيود و بيدي في الاخر يوزر لكل واحد» — Facebook's
--   rule): names are free to be alike or identical; every member gets a unique @username (0070_usernames.sql), and that tells two
--   members apart. It replaces the look-alike chase of rounds 1–8:
--   • the name's HYGIENE stays (Facebook's own name standards): letters of the Latin, Arabic, Greek or Cyrillic alphabet only (no
--     digits, symbols, emoji, invisible or format characters, no picker separator), one alphabet per word, a mark on its letter, the
--     bracket and spaced-dash display rules with their one-click suggestions; the eighth version's 'final' (ى / ں only at the end of
--     a word) served look-alikes only and is GONE — names it flagged are unflagged;
--   • profiles.name_key is no longer a look-alike skeleton (no TR39 prototypes, no pixel twins): it is the TYPING FOLD, for search —
--     every mark dropped (إ أ آ → ا, ؤ → و, é → e), a letter written with a hamza / madda / wasla is its letter (ArabicShaping.txt),
--     ة → ه, ى ی → ي, ک → ك, Latin / Greek / Cyrillic letters people type plainly as their plain letters (ø → o, ß → ss), punctuation,
--     spaces and a leading title dropped: «ابراهيم حسن» finds «إبراهيم حسن», «Jose» finds «José»;
--   • a new SEARCH-ONLY key, profiles.name_sound (person_name_sound — kept by the same trigger, trigram-indexed): the consonants of a
--     name as typed in Latin letters (Mohamed / Mohammed / Muhammad, Abdel / Abd El / Abdul, Youssef / Yusuf, Hussein / Hussain…);
--   • fix 9's real-name minors: names with ىء («هانىء»); a space on one side of a hyphen is refused ('dash', the message offers the
--     fix) instead of being joined silently; a zero-width space is removed where it draws nothing and a space where it breaks an
--     Arabic join; the 'word' refusal quotes what was typed.
--   The rule is generated, identical in the live app, by tools/names/name_rule.mjs (Unicode 16.0.0 data in tools/names/).
--   EXISTING NAMES: NOTHING IS RENAMED; a name the new rule refuses is FLAGGED (name_needs_fix), a name it now allows is unflagged,
--   every row is keyed again and gets its sound key. Counts: RAISE NOTICE.
-- Every function and table keeps or gets its GRANT/REVOKE (0026). Safe to run twice.
-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

